  "applies_to": "PVI XR10CX digital operating controls on RS-485 Modbus RTU, per PVI manual PV500-67 (06/2014).",
  "summary": "The XR10CX is a digital operating control used on PVI water heaters. It is a Modbus RTU slave on 2-wire RS-485 at a fixed 9600 8N1, with a handful of holding registers for temperature and set points and output coils for on/off, keypad lock, alarms and the call-for-heat relay.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The manual uses register numbers: holding register 40001 is address 0 on the wire, so subtract 40001 (40769 -> 768). Coils are numbered from 00001 the same way, so coil 513 is wire address 512."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "MODBUS-RTU Applied to the XR10CX Control",
    "doc_number": "PV500-67 06/2014",
    "revision_date": "2014-06",
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/PV500-67.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 4 (register numbering), p. 12 (Table 2), p. 13 (typical parameters, port setup)",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "PVI does not host this manual publicly that we could find; this copy is served by a controls distributor and is the unaltered PVI document (PVI Industries footer, document number on every page).",
    "Temperatures are whole degrees F per section 4.2.",
    "The manual is inconsistent about coil 513: Table 2 lists it as a Read/Write coil, while section 4.2 says ON/OFF is written as 257/1 and calls it write-only. Treat it as a standard on/off coil and confirm on site.",
    "Units for the differential and alarm delays are not stated in the table."
  ],
